WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.470
Lyme Regis, Dorset.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:07.410
Since 1957, a sea wall has stood
at the foot of the town's cliffs.

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:12.530
Before it, those cliffs eroded
about 0.45 metres a year.

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.810
Along the same coast, at
Slapton Sands in Devon,

5
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.950
the A379 road runs
along a shingle barrier,

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.170
with Slapton Ley behind.

7
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.350
The barrier is frequently
damaged in storms.

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.510
And here, the road is being let go.

9
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.510
Same coast, same sea.

10
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.450
So why treat them differently?

11
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.670
In this mission, you'll
weigh sea walls, revetments,

12
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.250
rip-rap, gabions and
groynes along this coast.

13
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.390
Then you'll test softer approaches,
and judge which can last.

14
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.310
Your mission: explain why Lyme Regis is
defended while the road at Slapton Sands

15
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.770
is being let go.
